# Unit 27 单词



## virtual
- **音标**: /ˈvɜːrtʃuəl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 虚拟的；实质上的
- **例句**: Virtual reality technology is becoming more popular.
- **近义词**: simulated, digital, near
- **派生词**: virtually (adv.)

## visible
- **音标**: /ˈvɪzəbl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 可见的；明显的
- **例句**: The stars are visible on a clear night.
- **近义词**: noticeable, apparent, observable
- **派生词**: visibility (n.), visibly (adv.), invisible (adj.)

## vital
- **音标**: /ˈvaɪtl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 至关重要的；生命的
- **例句**: Water is vital for survival.
- **近义词**: essential, crucial, critical
- **派生词**: vitality (n.), vitally (adv.)

## vivid
- **音标**: /ˈvɪvɪd/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 生动的；鲜明的
- **例句**: She has a vivid imagination.
- **近义词**: bright, lively, graphic
- **派生词**: vividly (adv.), vividness (n.)

## volume
- **音标**: /ˈvɑːljuːm/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 体积；音量；卷
- **例句**: The volume of traffic has increased significantly.
- **近义词**: amount, capacity, quantity
- **派生词**: voluminous (adj.)

## voluntary
- **音标**: /ˈvɑːlənteri/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 自愿的；志愿的
- **例句**: Participation in the program is voluntary.
- **近义词**: optional, willing, unpaid
- **派生词**: voluntarily (adv.), volunteer (n. v.), involuntary (反义)

## vote
- **音标**: /voʊt/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 投票；表决
- **例句**: Citizens have the right to vote in elections.
- **近义词**: ballot, poll, elect
- **派生词**: voter (n.), voting (n.)

## vow
- **音标**: /vaʊ/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 誓言；发誓
- **例句**: They made their wedding vows in front of family and friends.
- **近义词**: pledge, promise, oath
- **派生词**: vowed (adj.)

## vulnerable
- **音标**: /ˈvʌlnərəbl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 脆弱的；易受伤的
- **例句**: Children are particularly vulnerable to the disease.
- **近义词**: susceptible, exposed, defenseless
- **派生词**: vulnerability (n.), invulnerable (反义)

## wage
- **音标**: /weɪdʒ/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 工资；进行
- **例句**: The minimum wage has been raised this year.
- **近义词**: salary, pay, earnings
- **派生词**: wage (v.)

## wander
- **音标**: /ˈwɑːndər/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 漫步；迷路；离题
- **例句**: We wandered through the old town for hours.
- **近义词**: stroll, roam, stray
- **派生词**: wanderer (n.), wandering (n. adj.)

## warn
- **音标**: /wɔːrn/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 警告；提醒
- **例句**: The sign warns visitors not to touch the exhibits.
- **近义词**: alert, caution, notify
- **派生词**: warning (n. adj.), warner (n.)

## waste
- **音标**: /weɪst/
- **词性**: v. n. adj.
- **释义**: 浪费；废物
- **例句**: Don't waste your time on unimportant things.
- **近义词**: squander, garbage, useless
- **派生词**: wasteful (adj.), wasteland (n.)

## wave
- **音标**: /weɪv/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 波浪；挥手；浪潮
- **例句**: A wave of protests swept across the country.
- **近义词**: surge, ripple, gesture
- **派生词**: wavy (adj.)

## weakness
- **音标**: /ˈwiːknəs/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 弱点；缺点
- **例句**: One of her weaknesses is impatience.
- **近义词**: flaw, shortcoming, vulnerability
- **派生词**: weak (adj.), weaken (v.), weakly (adv.)

## wealth
- **音标**: /welθ/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 财富；丰富
- **例句**: He accumulated great wealth through hard work.
- **近义词**: riches, fortune, abundance
- **派生词**: wealthy (adj.)

## welfare
- **音标**: /ˈwelfer/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 福利；幸福
- **例句**: The government should protect the welfare of its citizens.
- **近义词**: well-being, benefit, prosperity

## whereas
- **音标**: /werˈæz/
- **词性**: conj.
- **释义**: 然而；鉴于
- **例句**: He is tall, whereas his brother is short.
- **近义词**: while, but, although

## widespread
- **音标**: /ˈwaɪdspred/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 广泛的；普遍的
- **例句**: There is widespread support for the new policy.
- **近义词**: extensive, prevalent, universal
- **派生词**: widely (adv.)

## willing
- **音标**: /ˈwɪlɪŋ/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 愿意的；乐意的
- **例句**: She is willing to help with the project.
- **近义词**: ready, eager, prepared
- **派生词**: willingly (adv.), willingness (n.), unwilling (adj.)

## wisdom
- **音标**: /ˈwɪzdəm/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 智慧；明智
- **例句**: With age comes wisdom.
- **近义词**: insight, knowledge, prudence
- **派生词**: wise (adj.), wisely (adv.)

## withdraw
- **音标**: /wɪðˈdrɔː/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 撤退；提取；退出
- **例句**: He decided to withdraw from the competition.
- **近义词**: pull out, remove, retreat
- **派生词**: withdrawal (n.), withdrawn (adj.)

## witness
- **音标**: /ˈwɪtnəs/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 目击者；见证
- **例句**: She witnessed the accident from her window.
- **近义词**: observer, spectator, see
- **派生词**: witnessed (adj.)

## wonder
- **音标**: /ˈwʌndər/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 奇迹；惊奇；想知道
- **例句**: The Great Wall is one of the wonders of the world.
- **近义词**: marvel, amazement, question
- **派生词**: wonderful (adj.), wonderfully (adv.)

## wrap
- **音标**: /ræp/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 包裹；缠绕
- **例句**: She wrapped the gift in colorful paper.
- **近义词**: cover, enclose, fold
- **派生词**: wrapper (n.), wrapping (n.)

## yield
- **音标**: /jiːld/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 产生；屈服；产量
- **例句**: The farm yields a good harvest every year.
- **近义词**: produce, surrender, output
- **派生词**: yielding (adj.)

## zone
- **音标**: /zoʊn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 地区；区域
- **例句**: This is a no-parking zone.
- **近义词**: area, region, district
- **派生词**: zoning (n.)

## abolish
- **音标**: /əˈbɑːlɪʃ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 废除；废止
- **例句**: The country abolished the death penalty in 2020.
- **近义词**: eliminate, eradicate, repeal
- **派生词**: abolition (n.), abolitionist (n.)

## abstract
- **音标**: /ˈæbstrækt/
- **词性**: adj. n. v.
- **释义**: 抽象的；摘要；提取
- **例句**: The concept of beauty is abstract.
- **近义词**: theoretical, summary, extract
- **派生词**: abstraction (n.), abstractly (adv.)

## accelerate
- **音标**: /əkˈseləreɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 加速；促进
- **例句**: The car accelerated as it entered the highway.
- **近义词**: speed up, hasten, quicken
- **派生词**: acceleration (n.)

## accommodate
- **音标**: /əˈkɑːmədeɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 容纳；提供住宿；适应
- **例句**: The hotel can accommodate up to 500 guests.
- **近义词**: house, lodge, adjust
- **派生词**: accommodation (n.)
